; bfsodium BYTEPAD168 : NIST SP 800_185's bytepad of two encoded strings
;
; NOTE square brackets are brainfuck loops  so comments use braces for counts;
;
; HAND WRITTEN skeleton; keccak/leftenc is PASTED twice and chacha20/add32 is
; PASTED twice  once inside each of the two doubling loops;
;
; INTERFACE entry=260 exit=264 footprint=0:483
; IO  in:  nlen{2} LE  slen{2} LE  nbuf{128}  sbuf{128}  one{1}  (261 bytes)
;     out: one block of 168 bytes
;
; ONE IS A FLAG AND NOUGHT IS THE ORDINARY CASE: nought encodes BOTH strings
; and one encodes only N  which is what KMAC's key block wants and what
;   bytepad( encode_string(K)  168 )
; means; The two string form appends encode_string of the empty string  which
; is the two bytes 01 00  and KMAC's answer is wrong by exactly those two;
; The flag is read LAST so that the cell is at nought for a caller that sends
; 260 bytes  which is why cSHAKE needed no change at all;
;
; This is  in the standard's own notation
;   bytepad( encode_string(N) then encode_string(S)  168 )
; which is what cSHAKE128 and KMAC128 put on the tape before the message;
; the 168 is SHAKE128's rate and it is in the file name because A RATE
; CANNOT BE A PARAMETER HERE: it sets the size of the block buffer  which is a
; tape map and not a number; the twin at the other rate is a separate file for
; the reason sponge136 and sponge168 are separate files;
;
; NLEN PLUS SLEN MUST BE AT MOST 160; the block holds two bytes for
; left_encode of the rate  then each string behind its own length encoding of
; two or three bytes  so the worst case is the rate less two less three less
; three; The routine DOES NOT CHECK IT  and a caller that breaks it pushes
; bytes off the end of the block;
;
; THE BLOCK IS BUILT RIGHT TO LEFT  BY PREPENDING  and that is the whole idea
; of this file; The standard's layout puts each piece at an offset that the
; lengths of the pieces before it decide  which is an index  which this
; library does not have; So the pieces go in BACKWARDS  last one first  and
; each one is put in by sliding the whole block right by its length and then
; ADDING it at cell nought; CELL NOUGHT IS ALWAYS CELL NOUGHT  so no position
; is ever computed;
;
; Two things fall out of that and both are wanted; the tail of the block is
; never written  so it stays at nought  which IS bytepad's padding; and the
; bytes of a string's buffer beyond its own length are nought  so adding a
; whole buffer over the top of the slid block cannot disturb what is already
; in front of it;
;
; EIGHT TIMES A LENGTH IS THREE DOUBLINGS; encode_string takes the length in
; BITS  and a doubling is chacha20/add32 with the accumulator as its own
; addend  so the multiply is a loop of three around a proved adder rather than
; a fourth hand rolled shift;
;
; TAPE MAP  (home @0)
;   @0x104        one     u8   one to encode N alone; nought for both
;   @0x105        dos     u8   the else arm of that flag
;   @0x000:0x001  nlen{2}  u16 LE  N's length in BYTES; its high byte is nought
;   @0x002:0x003  slen{2}  u16 LE  S's length in bytes
;   @0x004:0x083  nbuf{128} u8     N  as given; SPENT into the block
;   @0x084:0x103  sbuf{128} u8     S  as given; SPENT into the block
;   @0x108:@0x1af  block{168} u8  the answer  built from its right hand end
;   @0x1b4        k       u8   how many places the next prepend slides by
;   @0x1b5        t       u8   the cell a byte is copied through
;   @0x1b6        b       u8   and handed back through
;   @0x1b7        dbl     u8   the three doublings still to do
;   @0x1b8:@0x1bb  tmp{4}  u8   hands the accumulator back to itself
;   @0x1bc:@0x1cd  keccak/leftenc's frame  pasted at @0x1bc; footprint 0:17
;                 its x{4} is at @0x1bc  its count at @0x1c8  its bytes at @0x1c9
;   @0x1d0:@0x1e3  chacha20/add32's frame  pasted at @0x1d0; footprint 0:19
;                 its a{4} is the accumulator and its b{4} the addend

,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>   ; read the two lengths  the two buffers  and the one
  ,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>   ; string flag
  ,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>   ; continued
  ,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>   ; continued
  ,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>   ; continued
  ,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>   ; continued
  ,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>   ; continued
  ,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>   ; continued
  ,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,      ; continued
